# HakiOS fragment: the Qualcomm SM7150 family (SM7150, SM7150-AB "730G", SM7150-AC "732G"; "sdmmagpie") -- what is true of the
# SoC, whatever phone it is in.
#
# What is the same as the SC7280's, and so needs nothing here: the GICv3 (distributor 0x17a00000, redistributors 0x17a60000),
# the PMIC arbiter (version 5: core 0xc440000, cnfg 0xc40a000, observer 0xe600000), the cores numbered in MPIDR's second
# affinity field (0x000 to 0x700). The loader knows the SoC by UEFI's framebuffer at 0x9c000000 (xnuloader/loader.c,
# platform_sm7150) and gives the kernel cores 0-5 as the small ones.
#
# Eight cores, the kernel on core 7 (an A76): the ios-sweet port ran all eight on this SoC through PSCI (its patch 0078).
# CONFIG_CPUS=1 in a device's fragment, or cpus=1 on the command line, is the way back if a run stops while the cores start.
#
# What is NOT the SC7280's, and so left out: the processor clocks (OSM at 0x18321000, not EPSS: hakios.cpufreq.c is the
# SC7280's), the temperature sensors (TSENS at 0xc222000/0xc223000, not 0xc263000/0xc265000), the chip's identity
# (SMEM at 0x86000000 in this family's memory map; socinfo= needs soc_smem= first), the Adreno 618 (hakios.adreno.c is the
# 642L's), the modem and IPA (soc_* of their own, not yet read from the device tree).
CONFIG_SOC="sm7150"
CONFIG_CPUS=8
CONFIG_BOOTCPU=7
